{
  "result": "execscale_demo",
  "date": "2026-10-12",
  "question": "does one compiled chr21 programme RUN under the calibrated magnitude, and what does it emit?",
  "claim": "one compiled chr21 programme, emitted with the calibrated magnitude by compile_chromosome(magnitude='calibrated'), parses and RUNS under the multiplicative composition with the runtime reading the magnitude off the programme. What is reported is that it ran and what it emitted: the composed drive and the mRNA levels it produced, in arbitrary units, beside the same programme run at the compiled magnitude of 1.0",
  "does_not_claim": "this demo says NOTHING about RNA. No measured expression is read, nothing is fitted, no prediction is scored and no comparison to a measurement is made. Whether the calibrated composition is closer to measured RNA is M2h's result (`ac5580b`) and M2i's (`f6e71c6`) and is not re-read here. The magnitude is also a global AVERAGE over a magnitude that varies by chromosome (hetblock2, `d9e3ddd`), so running it on chr21 applies an average and not a chr21 number. The levels are arbitrary units from declared rates and a declared clamp, and are not expression",
  "magnitude": {
    "value": 0.2146,
    "source_commit": "ac5580b",
    "it_is_a_global_average": "+0.2146 is a global AVERAGE over a magnitude that is not one global number: hetblock2 (`d9e3ddd`) measured it varying by chromosome, surviving a locus-block null",
    "default_in_the_runtime": 1.0
  },
